# =============================================================================
# .env.example   (server)
# =============================================================================
# PURPOSE: A template for server/.env, which holds the server's settings.
# Commit THIS file, but NEVER commit .env (it's in .gitignore).
#
# WHAT TO BUILD: Under the TODOs below, add 3 lines in the form NAME=value,
# without "#" and with no spaces around "=". Leave the values blank in this
# example file, and put the real values in your own .env.
#
# TALKS TO: server.js loads .env with dotenv (process.env.NAME).
# NOTE: the Gemini key is NOT here. It lives in agent/.env, because only the
#       Python agent talks to Gemini.
#
# STEPS:
#   1. PORT=5000
#        The port Express listens on. client/vite.config.js proxies
#        /api to this port.
#   2. MONGO_URI=
#        Local:  mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/appname
#        Atlas:  mongodb+srv://<user>:<password>@<cluster>.mongodb.net/appname
#   3. AGENT_URL=http://localhost:8000
#        Where the Python agent runs. It must match AGENT_PORT in agent/.env.
#   4. Copy this file to server/.env and fill in the real values.
#
# CONCEPTS TO LEARN:
#   - Environment variables and process.env
#   - The dotenv package
#   - MongoDB connection strings (local vs Atlas)
# =============================================================================
